  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support access of vulnerable groups</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022; Implement integration activities to close gaps in community outreach and strengthen the capacity of provincial health workers;
&#x2022; Quickly implementation with a team of Oxfam and government partners who have a deep understanding of the local context, with a team in the project target areas, and highly skilled technical staff.
&#x2022; Strengthen local organizations through partnerships with local leaders and partners to the application of locally relevant approaches.
&#x2022; Implement the activities according to the plan stated in theMOU, under the supervision of Department of Hygiene and Health Promotion, and Provincial Health Department of respective target provinces.
&#x2022; Community Health and Inclusion Association (CHIAs) is responsible for project implementation and coordination with local authorities in districts of Saravan and Champasak provinces.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As of 11 March 2020, our organization has changed our name from Lao Positive Health Association (LaoPHA) to Community Health and Inclusion Association (CHIAs), as approved by the Ministry of Home Affairs, in order to broaden our mandates and more effectively respond to broader needs of our key affected communities. Our organization mandates have been focusing on strengthening community systemto advocate for Community-Led on Health, Nutrition, Rights and Genders for key diversity population, hard to reach groups and People Living with Diseases.
The Community Health &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; Inclusion Association was established under the name &#x2018;Lao Youth AIDS Project: LYAP&#x2019; in 1999 and later legally registered under the Association decree 238/PM, 2017.(Reg. No. 94/MOHA) in 2012under the name &#x2018;Lao Positive Health Association: LaoPHA&#x2019;. In 2020, the organization has rebranded itself to &#x2018;Community Health &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; Inclusion Association&#x201d; to reflect our current mandates that have become more diversified, which is to strengthen the communitysystems to advocate for community-led on health, community, rights and genders of vulnerable populations and the inclusion of key populations to take care of their health and social protection effectively by partnering with government agencies and international organizations. The emphasis is on vulnerable populations, including people with sexual diversity, women and children, migrant workers, people living with diseases, ethnic minorities and people inject drugs to be aware of their health, wellbeing and rights protection including being capable of effective response and effective access to relevant government&#x2019;s services.
Our Vision:
CHIAs&#x2019;s vision is to inspire inclusive communities where all key vulnerable populations and diverse groups take leadership to ensure improved health, individual rights and gender equality.
Our missions:
- Ensure all key vulnerable populations and diverse groups and people living with diseases have effective, affordable and equitable access to healthcare, rights and socialprotection;
- Ensure gender equality and sexual rights as well aseradicate violence, human trafficking and all forms of discriminations;
- Eradicate hunger and ensure adequate nutrition for all
- Strengthen partnership for development</narrative>
